In Ghana, local businesses range from low-capital street vending to capital-intensive manufacturing and agribusiness. Below is a categorized list of 100 local business ideas and their estimated startup or operation costs as of January 2026.
Regulatory Costs (Standard for all businesses)
Business Name Registration: GH₵50 – GH₵100
Company Registration (LLC): GH₵230 – GH₵350
Tax Identification Number (TIN): Free 
1. Micro-Businesses (Startup: GH₵100 – GH₵500)
These are typically "one-man" operations with minimal overhead. 
Sachet Water Sales: Buy in bulk and resell in traffic or kiosks.
Phone Credit/Data Transfer: Use EVD SIMs for commissions.
Shoe Polishing: Mobile service for offices and bus stops.
Running Errands: Personal shopping or delivery for busy professionals.
Boiled Egg & Pepper Sales: Highly popular street snack.
Banana & Groundnut Sales: Low-cost food retail.
Toffee & Candy Sales: Small-scale street vending.
Lawn Mowing/Weeding: Basic neighborhood maintenance.
Home Tutoring: Teaching primary or JHS students.
Book Editing: Freelance services for students or authors.
Social Media Profile Setup: Helping small shops get online.
Reviewing Products Online: Affiliate or freelance marketing.
Article/Content Writing: Ghostwriting for blogs.
Car Washing: Neighborhood-based mobile washing.
Customized Necktie Making: Small-scale fashion accessory.
Bead Making: Traditional and modern jewelry.
Snail Farming (Backyard): Initial GH₵1,000 for large scale, but can start for GH₵500.
Laundry Services: Basic hand-wash services for neighbors.
Mobile Notary: Low-cost service if certified.
Virtual Assistant: Administrative help for remote clients. 
